 in the last three years to help the States to take-up SLWM \nProjects. Under SBM-G, component-wise funds are not released. Howe ver,  State/UT-wise central \nshare released under Nirmal Bharat Abhiyaan (NBA)/SBM (G) du ring the last 3 years and the \ncurrent year is at Annexure-1. \n(b) Three regional workshops were organized at Trivandrum, Guwahati and Ranchi during 2014-15. \nA National workshop on SLWM was organized in New Delhi on 21.04.2015. Thre e Exhibitions \nwere organized in New Delhi on 26-27 th  August 2014, 23-24 January 2015 and 2-3 July 2015 \nwherein  innovative technologies in respect of Solid and Liquid Waste M anagement were \nshowcased to various State Governments.    \n(c) Under SBM-G, component-wise funds are not released. However, St ate/UT may take-up \nSLWM projects as per SBM(G) Guidelines. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-1 \nStatement referred in part (a) of the reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.170 due for reply on 5-\n05-2016 \nState/UT-wise, Central share released during last 3 years and current year under NBA / SBM(G) \n(Rs. in Crore) \nState/UT 2013-14 2014-15 2015- 16                               2016-17(Upto \n30-4-2016)                               \nA & N ILANDS 0 0 3.40   \nANDHRA PRADESH  145.24 116.10 234.17   \nARUNACHAL PRADESH  5.19 14.61 38.71 4.73 \nASSAM  41.81 185.78 187.67   \nBIHAR  0.00 0.00 182.14   \nCHHATTISGARH  0.00 28.12 144.72 77.96 \nD & N HAVELI  0.00 0.00 0.00   \nGOA  0.00 0.00 1.05   \nGUJARAT  52.64 156.07 478.22   \nHARYANA  131.18 5.93 29.53   \nHIMACHAL PRADESH  30.50 130.17 4.37   \nJAMMU & KASHMIR  39.57 103.08 4.05   \nJHARKHAND  0.00 23.05 97.32 81.18 \nKARNATAKA  65.95 312.57 335.45   \nKERALA  43.01 33.97 8.50   \nMADHYA PRADESH  660.39 0.00 220.28   \nMAHARASHTRA  36.46 236.11 567.45   \nMANIPUR  0.00 9.18 44.19 27.27 \nMEGHALAYA  103.04 0.00 35.65 41.22 \nMIZORAM  8.06 0.00 3.32   \nNAGALAND  0.00 20.87 10.83   \nODISHA  0.00 65.84 56