SWERED ON MAY 04, 2016 \nAFFORDABLE HOUSING \n \nNo. 145*    DR. KULMANI SAMAL: \n  SHRI KIRTI AZAD:   \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY \nALLEVIATION be pleased to state: \n(a) the cities selected under Phase1 of the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana \nfor construction of affordable houses, State-wise; \n(b) whether the target of finalising 100 cities to be covered under Phase 1 \nhas been met; \n(c) if so, the number of houses constructed or under construction in the \nfirst phase of the scheme;  \n(d) whether the Government is maintaining specific quality standards for \nthe construction of the houses and if so, the details thereof; and \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor and the corrective action taken in this \nregard? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n[SHRI M. VENKAIAH NAIDU] \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the Sabha.  \n******  \n \n \nContd/-…2... \n  \n\n-2- \n \nSTATEMENT \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 145* FOR 04.05.2016 REGARDING “AFFORDABLE \nHOUSING” \n  \n(a) & (b): As on 25.04.2016, total 2508 cities of 26 States have been \nidentified and selected for Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Housing for All \n(Urban) Mission. State-wise list of 2508 cities/towns is at Annexure-1.  \n(c) : Details of houses constructed under PMAY(U) mission are at \nAnnexure-2. \n(d) & (e): As per the scheme guidelines, the houses under the PMAY \n(U) mission should be designed and constructed to meet the \nrequirement of structural safety against earthquakes, flood, cyclone, \nlandslide etc. confirming to the National Building Code and other \nrelevant Bureau of Indian Standards (BIS) codes.  \nThe mission also includes a Technology Sub-Mission to facilitate State \n/ City Governments to adopt modern, innovative and green \ntechnologies for adoption of layout designs and building plans suitable \nfor various geo-climatic zones and to deploy disaster resistant and \nenvironment friendly technologies.\n  \n****** \n \n\nS. \nNo. CITY S. \nNo. CITY\n1 Adoni 31 Nandyal\n2 Amadalavalasa 32 Narasaraopet\n3 Amalapuram 33 Nellimarla\n4 Amaravati 34 Nellore\n5 Anantapur 35 Ongole\n6 Atmakur 36 Palacole\n7 Bhimavaram 37 Palasa Kasibugga\n8 Bobbili 38 Parvathipuram\n9 Chilakaluripet 39 Peddapuram\n10 Chirala 40 Pithapuram\n11 Chittoor 41 Ponnur\n12 Dharmavaram 42 Proddatur\n13 Eluru 43 Rajahmundry\n14 Gudivada 44 Ramachandrapuram\n15 Gudur 45 Rayachoti\n16 Guntakal 46 Rayadurg\n17 Guntur 47 Salur\n18 Hindupur 48 Samalkota\n19 Kadapa 49 Sattenapalle\n20 Kadiri 50 Srikakulam\n21 Kakinada 51 Srikalahasti\n22 Kandukur 52 Tadepalligudem\n23 Kavali 53 Tadipatri\n24 Kurnool 54 Tenali\n25 Machilipatnam 55 Tirupati\n26 Madanapalle 56 Tuni\n27 Mandapeta 57 Vijayawada\n28 Mangalagiri 58 Visakhapatanam\n29 Markapur 59 Vizianagaram\n30 Mydukur 60 Yemmiganur\n1 Aalo 16 Miao\n2 Anini 17 Naharlagun\n3 Basar 18 Namsai\n4 Boleng 19 Pasighat\n5 Bomdila 20 Roing\n6 Changlang 21 Sagalee\n7 Daporijo 22 Seppa\n8 Deomali 23 Tawang\n9 Dirang 24 Tezu\n10 Hawai 25 Yingkiong\n11 Itanagar 26 Ziro\n12 Jairampur 27 Dumporijo\n13 Khonsa 28 Mariyang\n14 Koloriang 29 Palin\n15 Longding\nAnnexure referred in reply to Lok sabha Stared question no 145*  \nfor 04-05-2016 regarding \"Affordable Housing\"\n[as on 25th April 2016]\nAndhra Pradesh\nArunachal Pradesh\nAnnexure - I\n\nS. \nNo. CITY S. \nNo. CITY\nAnnexure referred in reply to Lok sabha Stared question no 145*  \nfor 04-05-2016 regarding \"Affordable Housing\"\n[as on 25th April 2016]\nAnnexure - I\n1 Amarpur 71 Khagaria\n2 Araria 72 Khagaul\n3 Areraj 73 Kharagpur\n4 Arrah 74 Khusrupur\n5 Arwal 75 Kishanganj\n6 Aurangabad 76 Koath\n7 Bagaha 77 Kochas\n8 Bahadurganj 78 Koilwar\n9 Bairgania 79 Lakhisarai\n10 Bakhri 80 Lalganj\n11 Bakhtiarpur 81 Madhepura\n12 Balia 82 Madhubani\n13 Banka 83 Maharajganj\n14 Banmankhi Bazar 84 Mahnar Bazar\n15 Barahiya 85 Mahua\n16 Barauli 86 Mairwa\n17 Barbigha 87 Makhdumpur\n18 Barh 88 Maner\