roject affected people are \ndecided by the project authorities as per existing R &R policy of Centre/State whichever is \nmore beneficial. \n \nAs per information available with the Central Water Commission (CWC), State -wise and \nproject-wise list of number of displaced persons in respect of Major & Medium Irrigation \nProjects is enclosed.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure as referred to in reply to part (a) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No.171 due for reply on 05.05.2016 regarding \n                                                 Rehabilitation of Displaced Families Due to Irrigation Projects \nProject-wise number of displaced persons in respect of Major & Medium Irrigation Projects \nAndhra Pradesh   \nSl.No. Name of Project Number of displaced people \n1 Srisailam 110097 \n2 Nagarjunasagar 24500 \n3 Yeleru 10121 \n4 Somasila 100000 \n5 Telguganga 16982 \n6 Vamsadhara st-II Hiramandalam(Niradi Barrage) 13622 \n7 Priyadarshini Jurala 8645 \n8 Vengalarasagram 133 \n9 Maddidedda Reservoir 75 \n10 Sriram Sagar 150000 \n11 Annamaya( cheyyeru) 500 \n12 Kandalleru Reservoir 30000 \n TOTAL 464675 \nAssam   \n1 Lower Subansiri H.E. project 443 \n TOTAL 443 \nBihar   \n1 North Koel Reservoir 3368 \n2 Durgavati Reservoir 2500 \n TOTAL 5868 \nChhattisgarh   \n1 Sondur Reservoir( Mahanadi Reservoir) 1516 \n2 Barnal Project 153 \n3 Hasedo Bango ( Mini Mata) 13605 \n4 Kosarteda Medium Irrigationn Project 3695 \n5 Ravi Sankar Sagar Reservir 21495 \n6 Kelo Major 1736 \n7 Dudhawa Reservoir 9437 \n8 Chhirpani 225 \n9 Rani Rasmi Tank 134 \n10 Kharkhara Tank 6568 \n11 Matiamoti tank 3438 \n12 Sutiyapat Medium project 452 \n13 Kara Nala 296 \n14 Sukha Nala 142 \n TOTAL 62892 \nGoa   \n1 Anjunem 1460 \n TOTAL 1460 \nGujarat   \n1 Sardar Sarovar 18000 \n2 Kadana 16151 \n3 Ukai 16000 \n4 Panam 17491 \n5 Damanganga 11805 \n6 Sipu reservoir 7225 \n7 Wetrak Reservoir 15670 \n8 Sabarmati reservoir 15745 \n9 Karjan eservoir 8025 \n10 Venu-II 2416 \n\n \n11 Demi-II 51