 \nDevelopment of Technic al Textiles, Schemes for the Development of the Powerloom \nSector, Integrated Scheme for Powerloom Sector Development (ISPSD), Scheme for \nIntegrated Textile Parks (SITP), Schemes for Development of Silk and Sericulture \nsectors, National Handloom Development  Programme (NHDP), Comprehensive \nHandloom Cluster Development Scheme(CHCDS), Yarn supply Scheme etc. The \nGovernment of India has recently notified the Amended Technology Upgradation Fund \nScheme (A-TUFS) for technology Upgradation in  the textiles sectors. T hese schemes \nare aimed at promoting textile industry all over the country including Maharashtra . An \noutlay of Rs. 25931 crores has been made for Textiles sector d uring the current Five \nYear Plan (2012 to 2017).   Scheme wise funds spent during the last thr ee years (2013-\n14, 2014-15 and 2015-16) are given in Annexure-I. The details of foreign assistance \nprovided for textile units including those in Maharashtra are not available. The details \nof state - wise expenditure for  important initiatives and schemes in the Powerloom \nSector is at Annexure-II. Details of State -wise financial assistance released for \ntechnology upgradation for Block level Clusters programme under National Handloom \nDevelopment Programme (NHDP) and Comprehensive Handloom Development \nScheme (CHDS) is at Annexure- III and IV respectively. \n \n \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nDetails of plans funds spent in respect of schemes relating to various segments of the \nTextile sector during each of the last three financial years (2013-14 to 2015-16). \n        Rs in Crores \nSr.No. Name of the Scheme / Sector 2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 \n1 2 4 5 6 \n1 Handloom 550.00 397.44 549.19 \n2 Handicraft 142.13 100.99 163.66 \n3 Wool & Woollens 16.66 20.00 27.51 \n4 Sericulture / Silk 374.55 297.58 178.10 \n5 Powerlooms 13.09 51.52 101.02 \n6 Megacluster 38.75 61.79 138.75 \n7 Industry schemes including \nTechnology Upgradation Fund \nScheme (TUFS),  Scheme for \nIntegrated Textiles Park (SITP), \nIntegrated Skill Development \nSchemes (ISDS) and North East \nRegion Textile Promotion \nScheme (NERTPS) \n2029.78 2384.39 1951.27 \n  GRAND TOTAL  3164.96 3313.71 3109.50 \n\nAnnexure-II \nPowerloom Sector initiatives / Schemes \nState-wise and Scheme-wise Physical and Financial achievment for the year 2015-16 (as on 31.03.16) \n  \n                                        \nS.No State \nGWS GIS In-situ MMS - TUFS BSM Exposure Visit Seminar/ \nWorkshop \nYarn \nBank \nCommon Facility \nCenter (CFC) \nNo. of \nprojects \nRs. in \ncrore \nNo. of \nworkers \nenrolled \nRs. in \ncrore \nNo. of \nlooms \nupgraded \nRs. in \ncrore \nNo. of \ncases \nRs. in \ncrore \nNo. of \nmeets \nRs. in \ncrore \nNo. of \nweavers \nRs. in \ncrore \nNo. of \nprogram\nmes \nRs. in \ncrore \nNo. of \nprojects \nRs. in \ncrore \nNo. \nof \nproj\nects \nRs. \nin \ncror\ne \n1 Andhra \nPradesh           -              -            \n4,428  \n       \n0.13         1,539               4            \n1.34  \n           \n4        0.40           54      0.016             2      0.005            -              -                  \n-    \n            \n-    \n2 Assam           -              -                 \n74  \n       \n0.00              -                -                  \n-    \n           \n1        0.08            -              -               1      0.010            -              -                  \n-    \n            \n-    \n3 Bihar           -              -            \n1,667  \n       \n0.05                3              -                  \n-    \n          \n-              -             47      0.014             1      0.006            -              -                  \n-    \n            \n-    \n4 Chhattisgarh           -              -                  \n-    \n           \n-                -                - "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|8|UNSTARRED |76", "t": "IIT Graduates", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  *76 (16 th  Position)  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 28-4-2016  \n \nSanitary Complexes \n \n*76. SHRI KESINENI NANI: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the funds generated through Swachh Bharat Cess so far, State-wise; \n \n(b) the criteria/structure for disbursal of these funds/cess to the States/UTs; \n \n(c) the financial assistance provided to various State Governm ents including Andhra Pradesh under \nSwachh Bharat Mission (SBM) during each of the last three yea rs and the current year, State/UT-\nwise; \n \n(d) the steps taken for total sanitation of villages through the c onstruction of drains soaked pits, \nsolid and liquid waste disposal under SBM in Andhra Pradesh; and \n \n(e) the number of sanitary complexes for women with facilitie s for sanitation, bathing and washing \nconstructed in Andhra Pradesh under SBM? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  \n(SHRI BIRENDER SINGH) \n \n \n \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.  *76 for 28.4.2016. \n \n(a) The total amount collected under Swachh Bharat Cess (SBC) dur ing mid-November 2015 to \nMarch 2016 is Rs. 3900 crore (provisional gross figure). The State-w ise data in this regard is not \nmaintained by Central Board of Excise & Customs, Department of Revenue.  \n \n(b) \nFunds collected under the Cess will be distributed between the tw o Sub-Missions i.e. Swachh \nBharat Mission (Gramin) and Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban) in the ratio of 80:20 respectively and \nutilized as per the guidelines and components of Swachh Bharat Mis sion (Gramin) and Swachh \nBharat Mission (Urban).  \n \n(c) State/UT-wise, Central share released during last 3 ye ars and current year  to various State \nGovernments including Andhra Pradesh under Nirmal Bharat Abhiyan (NBA ) (upto 1 st  October, \n2014) / Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) (from 2 nd  October, 2014) is at Annexure-1.  State/UT-\nwise, Central share released during last 3 years and current y ear  to various State Governments \nincluding Andhra Pradesh under Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban) is at Annexure-2. \n \n(d) The Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) has been launched on 2nd Octob er, 2014, which aims at \nattaining Swachh Bharat by 2 nd  October 2019. Solid and Liquid Waste Management (SLWM) is \none of the integral component of SBM(G) and under this component, activi ties like compost pits, \nvermi composting, biogas plants, low cost drainage, soakage channel s/ pits, reuse of waste water \nand system for collection, , segregation and disposal of household garbag e and menstrual hygiene \nmanagement etc. can be taken up. Funds for Solid and Liquid Waste Ma nagement activities with \ncap of Rs. 7/12/15/20 lakh are available for Gram Panchayats having upto 150/300/500/ more than \n500 households.  \n \n(e) 10  Community Sanitary Complexes have been constructed in Andhra Prades h under Swachh \nBharat Mission(Gramin) since 2.10.2014.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-1 \nStatement referred in part (d) of the reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.76 due for reply on 28-\n04-2016 \nState/UT-wise, Central share released during last 3 years and current year under NBA / SBM(G)* \n(Rs. in Crore) \nState/UT 2013-14 2014-15 2015- 16                               2016-17(Upto \n25-4-2016)                               \nA & N ILANDS 0 0 3.40   \nANDHRA PRADESH  145.24 116.10 234.17   \nARUNACHAL PRADESH  5.19 14.61 38.71 4.73 \nASSAM  41.81 185.78 187.67   \nBIHAR  0.00 0.00 182.14   \nCHHATTISGARH  0.00 28.12 144.72 77.96 \nD & N HAVELI  0.00 0.00 0.00   \nGOA  0.00 0.00 1.05   \nGUJARAT  52.64 156.07 478.22   \nHARYANA  131.18 5.93 29.53   \nHIMACHAL PRADESH  30.50 130.17 4.37   \nJAMMU & KASHMIR  39.57 103.08 4.05   \